 stat:"More than 50 kinds of Hawaiian honeycreepers evolved from one kind of finch",
 body:"Their beaks went every way: long and curved like the ʻiʻiwi’s for sipping flowers, thick like the palila’s for seeds, and the ʻakiapōlāʻau has a woodpecker-like lower beak and a long curved upper one, like a Swiss army knife.",
